# Blue Shift HD snark. Measured by vrcardgen from
#   bshift_hd/models/v_squeak.mdl
# finished by hand.
#
# Part J: "Take one from the nest on the chest. It squirms in the hand and
# bites if held too long (a small amount of damage, the Half-Life way).
# Throw it, or drop it at your feet and let it hunt."
#
# So: nothing to work, nothing to load, nothing to aim. The card says the
# weapon is released and then stops talking, because after the release the
# snark is a monster and not a weapon.
#
# WHY THERE ARE NO JOINTS, measured rather than assumed. This rig is two
# skeletons in one model: Bip01 (bones 0-41, 40.1% of the mesh) is the
# player's arm and hand, and Bip02 (bones 42-56, 59.9%) is the snark itself,
# parented to `Bip01 R Finger1` - the creature hangs off the index finger of
# the fist that holds it. vrcardgen finds six drivable bones in the Bip02
# subtree and they are all anatomy:
#
#   Bip02 Neck      1.89 rad   Bip02 Head       1.83 rad
#   Bip02 L UpperArm 2.34 rad  Bip02 L Forearm  1.76 rad
#   Bip02 R UpperArm 1.68 rad  Bip02 R Forearm  1.91 rad
#
# Every one of those is pure rotation with zero translation, and none of
# them appears in `throw`. Posing the six sequences says what they are:
#
#   idle1       the creature almost still - head 2 deg, neck 6 deg
#   fidgetfit   the squirm: neck 108 deg, head 93 deg, legs 179 deg
#   fidgetnip   the BITE: head 91 deg, thighs 193/181 deg - it twists
#               round in the fist to reach the hand
#   down / up   holster and draw
#   throw       ONE bone moves: Bip02 translates 129.43 units, and not a
#               single joint in the creature rotates at all
#
# A neck that turns 108 degrees while the thing squirms is not a degree of
# freedom the hand drives; it is the model breathing. Declaring any of it as
# a joint would hand the simulator a hand-spring on the snark's skull. The
# squirming and the biting belong to Part I (a thing in the hand with its own
# behaviour) and Part G (haptics), not to a mechanism. Hence: no joints.
#
# NO ATTACHMENTS AT ALL on this model - numattachments is 0, so there is no
# muzzle and no eject position to record. Correct for a thrown weapon: the
# release direction comes from the hand's own velocity (Part F-05), not from
# a barrel axis. The 129-unit arc in `throw` is Half-Life's canned flight
# path and the VR build replaces it with the real throw.
#
# Weapon extent 16.39 units, from vertices - the header bounding boxes on
# this model are (0,0,0) like every other retail valve model.

weapon v_squeak
match  bones 57  seqs 6  hash 0xab512ff3

# The bone every position in this card is measured in - the controls, the
# grab points, the chamber, the ejection port. Nothing recorded it until
# the engine had to place a control in the world to ask whether a thumb is
# near it; the simulator never needed one, because it never works in world
# space. Taken from the generator, which has always called this bone the
# WEAPON BODY and is what measured these numbers in the first place.
body   "Bip02 Spine"

type   thrown
fuse   0           # it is alive; it decides
